<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		The abaddon's abdomen draws over her right wing in the north view (user's report,
		2026-10-03: "the abdomen is displaying in front of the wing").

		Two mods set the depth of the two things, and they only collide in that one view:

		  * VRE's cosmetic spawning sack is a render node under the Body tag, layer -3 in every
		    view but the north one, which carries 90.
		  * Big & Small's wing tracker draws the wings at -2, -1 and 92. Its right back wing has
		    no north override, so it keeps -2 and the sack's 90 lands on top of it. The matching
		    left back wing is `visibleFacing East` and is not drawn in the north view at all,
		    which is why the report names the right wing alone.

		The first attempt lowered the sack's north layer to -3, the value its own other three
		views use. It was deployed and loaded (the game started after it, and the log shows no
		patch failure) and the user still saw the abdomen over the wing, so this goes at the
		wing instead - the side the request actually asks to move.

		90.5 is the value and every digit matters: above the sack's 90, and below the near
		wings' 91 and 92, so the far wing draws over the abdomen while staying behind the wings
		on the near side. `PawnRenderNodeWorker.LayerFor` feeds `AltitudeForLayer`, which is what
		orders the pawn's draw requests, so a layer is the right lever. The change is per pawn
		and per facing: the north view alone. Other winged pawns keep the relative order they
		always had (-2, -1, 92 becomes 90.5, -1, 92).

		Both back-wing nodes are given it. Only the right one is drawn in the north view today,
		but the rule is written for the pair so a version that widens `visibleFacing` still
		behaves.

		Gated on Big and Small by display name: the xpath can only match that mod's tracker, and
		a patch operation that matches nothing is an error in the log.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
		<mods>
			<li>Big and Small - Framework</li>
		</mods>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>Defs/*[defName="BS_HumanoidWithWings_Race"]/renderNodeProperties/li[conditionalGraphics/conditionalPaths/altDefs/li="BS_FeatheredWingBack"]/drawData</xpath>
			<value>
				<dataNorth>
					<layer>90.5</layer>
				</dataNorth>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>
</Patch>
